## Finding R1 (P2): validate the expected RED failure before exempting its text from warning checks

`oracle.py:44` accepts any nonempty `detail` string when the record is labelled `site=P011, kind=fail`. `warning_log` at lines 77–80 then removes that entire string from the combined logs before testing for warnings, world-age/method-overwrite messages, errors, or other failures. Thus neither the expected P011 expression/source/rendering nor the absence of warnings within the exempted text is established.

Fresh independent fixtures with exact RED totals, exact named-site counts/tree, all nine valid payload files, valid decisions, and identical raw/unit records were accepted when the sole P011-labelled detail contained (a) an unrelated assertion expression, (b) the nominal failure followed by `WARNING: method overwriting`, or (c) arbitrary nonempty text. In each case `oracle.validate` succeeds and `warning_log` returns false for the matching log. The 759-check independent script records these as three failing negative expectations; its other 756 checks pass. The full auditor calls these two functions without an additional failure-detail check, so it does not repair this gap.

This contradicts the stated requirement to remove only a validated expected P011 rendering and reject other warnings/errors. Validate a bounded, phase-specific expected P011 failure representation, including the frozen source/assertion identity and allowed nonzero allocation result, before exempting only that rendering. Do not hard-code 208 bytes. Embedded warning/error/extra-failure lines and unrelated expressions must remain rejected. Preserve the original RED test body and fixed copied recorder unless a separately reviewed amendment explicitly changes those constraints. This finding concerns saved-evidence validation; it does not claim the frozen Julia driver actually emits the synthetic malformed details.

